      "text": "To determine how many integers Josef can pick such that Timothy's quotient is an integer, we need to find the divisors of 1000. An integer \\( d \\) is a divisor of 1000 if and only if \\( \\frac{1000}{d} \\) is an integer. Therefore, we need to find all the divisors of 1000.\n\nFirst, we perform the prime factorization of 1000:\n\\[ 1000 = 10^3 = (2 \\cdot 5)^3 = 2^3 \\cdot 5^3. \\]\n\nThe formula to find the number of divisors of a number \\( n = p_1^{e_1} \\cdot p_2^{e_2} \\cdot \\ldots \\cdot p_k^{e_k} \\) is \\( (e_1 + 1)(e_2 + 1) \\cdots (e_k + 1) \\). Applying this to our prime factorization of 1000:\n\\[ (3+1)(3+1) = 4 \\cdot 4 = 16. \\]\n\nThus, there are 16 divisors of 1000. This means Josef can pick any of these 16 integers. The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]",
